# Taz_6_2d_3
{1820}{}{The ranch was growing quickly, but it was still relatively small. They were short on labor, so they hired anyone willing to work. The farmers taught me the basics, and I honed my skills over the years.}

# Taz_7_1
{1850}{}{We no longer breed brahma here. The brahmin you see come from other settlements. Porto's land serves as a large holding pen for them, like a staging point before they are either butchered or moved as livestock to our customers.}
{1851}{}{Which places does Tibbets, umm... "Porto", sell its produce to?}
{1852}{}{Why do the cattle traders bring their brahmin here instead of taking them directly to their customers?}

# Taz_7_2a_1
{1880}{}{Well, people have come to appreciate the wisdom of the Freeroaming Brahmin Traders' concept.}
{1881}{}{Who are they?}

# Taz_7_2a_2
{1910}{}{They're run by Hofferman and are based here. They handle the consolidation of nearly all the brahmin raised in this area for the market in Porto. Selling them wholesale brings in more profit.}
{1911}{}{I see the logic in that. Can I ask you another question?}
{1912}{}{Understood. I have to be going now, Taz. Take care.}

