# Taz_7_2b_5
{2120}{}{[He leans towards you, speaking in a low voice.] The Freeroaming Brahmin Traders are a completely legitimate organization... nowadays.}
{2121}{}{Go on.}

# Taz_7_2b_6
{2150}{}{They started differently, though. You see, they had to convince all the brahmin traders in this area to stockpile their cattle in Porto and join the Freeroaming Brahmin Traders syndicate.}
{2151}{}{What was the purpose of that?}
{2152}{}{What's wrong with that?}

# Taz_7_2b_7a
{2180}{}{If you have lots of brahmin in one convenient place, you can drive them in one big run to your customers instead of small quantities. It reduces costs and increases profits.}
{2181}{}{And why is that seen as a bad thing?}
{2182}{}{I see. Let me ask you about something else instead.}

# Taz_7_2b_7b_1
{2210}{}{Well, this is where it gets tricky. Not all the farmers and traders in this area wanted to join the Freeroaming Brahmin Traders. Hofferman wasn't one to take no for an answer, and things turned ugly a few times.}
{2211}{}{Ugly? How so?}

# Taz_7_2b_7b_2
{2240}{}{There were rumors at the time that Hofferman resorted to intimidation and brahmin rustling, with the help of Porto's gangs. Those who refused to join had their brahmin stolen from them.}
{2241}{}{That's a serious accusation!}
{2242}{}{Why was Hofferman so determined to compel the other traders to join his group?}

# Taz_7_2b_7b_3
{2270}{}{Damn right it is! And you never heard it from me. Like I said, those were just rumors.}
{2271}{}{So, why was Hofferman so eager to force the other traders into his organization?}
{2272}{}{Let's change the subject. Do you have time for another question?}
{2273}{}{I'd better leave you to it, Taz. Take care.}

